	<tr>
		<td valign="top" class="headline8" colspan="2">Bush Spokesman Calls Notion That U.S. Went to War Over Disputed Uranium Claim a 'Bunch of Bull'</td>
		<td valign="top" rowspan="3" width="95" class="imagecredit8"><a href="/news/data/11_ds_153661.asp"><img src="/dsdsmultimedia/photos/FLEISCHER_STEPS_DOWN.jpg" width="85" border="0"></a></td>
	</tr>
	<tr>
		<td valign="top" colspan="2" class="citation8">The White House sought to put to rest questions over President Bush's disputed claim that Iraq sought African uranium, saying Monday that such fears were not a major component in Bush's case for war.&nbsp;&nbsp;<a href="/news/data/11_ds_153661.asp">Full Story</a>
		</td>
	</tr>
	<tr>
		<td valign="top" class="imagecredit8">AP Photo &#150; J. SCOTT APPLEWHITE
