	<tr>
		<td valign="top" class="headline8" colspan="2">France Celebrates Bastille Day; Leaders Say U.N. Inspectors Could Settle Iraqi Arms Dispute</td>
		<td valign="top" rowspan="3" width="95" class="imagecredit8"><a href="/news/data/11_ds_153456.asp"><img src="/dsdsmultimedia/photos/FRANCE_BASTILLE_DAY11.jpg" width="85" border="0"></a></td>
	</tr>
	<tr>
		<td valign="top" colspan="2" class="citation8">French leaders used their traditional Bastille Day interviews Monday to press for the return of U.N. weapons inspectors to Iraq, saying such a move could help settle the doubts over Saddam Hussein's weapons of mass murder.&nbsp;&nbsp;<a href="/news/data/11_ds_153456.asp">Full Story</a>
		</td>
